{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1453135255,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxMjcyNjQ1MDU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/338","origin":"github"},"title":"get_contentlocation within archive.py special remote -- unnecessary invocations","message":"Originally since batching of contentlocation to annex doesn't yet work, but probably a desired feature overall.  Some annex calls could be memoized or cached to significantly improve performance by minimizing interaction with annex.  E.g. in the case of archives special remote it needs frequently to determine the physical location for the tarballs within .git/annex/objects but that location doesn't change at all through the invocations.  The only thing which could change is the availability of that archive.  So, as a first measure, I will create a simple cached version for get_contentlocation specifically within AnnexCustomRemote but it might be desired to generalize over to AnnexRepo at some point.\n\nAlso initiating this issue to check task/context feature of pycharm: https://www.jetbrains.com/pycharm/help/managing-tasks-and-context.html  which I hope start using","files":null}]}